  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Energy of Hydrogen like atoms is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>eV</mi></math>.</p><p>Since Helium is in the first state,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>The energy of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ion is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
